# Confirmations — ConfirmModal only

User confirmations (delete, irreversible actions, “are you sure?”) use the **global Metronic modal**, not `window.confirm` or `alert`.

## Stack

- `ConfirmModal` in [`resources/js/components/ConfirmModal.vue`](resources/js/components/ConfirmModal.vue) — mounted in [`AdminDashboardLayout.vue`](resources/js/Pages/Layouts/AdminDashboardLayout.vue)
- `useConfirmModal()` in [`resources/js/composables/useConfirmModal.js`](resources/js/composables/useConfirmModal.js)

## Do

```javascript
import { useConfirmModal } from '@/composables/useConfirmModal';

const confirmModal = useConfirmModal();

const onDelete = async (item) => {
    const confirmed = await confirmModal.confirm({
        title: 'Delete category',
        message: 'Delete "' + item.name + '"? This cannot be undone.',
        confirmLabel: 'Delete',
        cancelLabel: 'Cancel',
        variant: 'danger',
    });

    if (!confirmed) {
        return;
    }

    router.delete('/categories/' + item.id, { preserveScroll: true });
};
```

- Use `variant: 'danger'` for destructive actions; `variant: 'primary'` (default) for neutral confirms
- Keep `confirmModal.confirm()` **async** and return early when the user cancels
- Add `ConfirmModal` to any **new staff layout** that needs confirmations (same pattern as `FlashGrowl`)

## Do not

- `window.confirm()`, `window.alert()`, or browser `prompt()`
- Inline one-off modal markup duplicated per page — reuse `useConfirmModal`
- Custom confirm toasts for yes/no decisions (toasts are for feedback after an action; see flash-growl rule)

## New destructive actions

When adding delete/remove/cancel-with-loss flows in admin Vue pages, wire them through `useConfirmModal` with a clear title, specific message, and labeled buttons.
